<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Select by Curvature</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p>This command is accessible from <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select &gt; Mesh &gt; By Curvature</b></span>.</p>
<p class="description"><span lang="EN-GB" class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Select By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">computes the curvature per visible point comparing it's normal and it's neighbour's normal, decides whether it is a curved or a flat surface and selects it. It also removes isolated regions of like-coloured connected triangles, which are probably noise. This command works on meshes only.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature.gif" width="223px" height="249px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Neighbours</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Level of neighbourhood. See</span> <u><span lang="EN-GB"><a href="Point_Curvature.htm">Point Curvature</a></span></u> <span lang="EN-GB">for details. Higher values will cause selection of flatter surface. Use higher level for noisy surfaces. Range of this parameter is from 1 to 5. Default values is Neighbours = 1.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP225903816" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="margin-left:23.4pt; border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_neighbour_1.gif" width="237px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_neighbour_3.gif" width="238px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs8" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Neighbours = 1</span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Neighbours = 3</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Flatness</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Angle threshold for the greatest angle between the normals of every vertex and the vertices from the chosen neighbourhood level. Lower values will cause selection of flatter surface. Range of this parameter is from 1 to 180. Default values is Flatness = 8.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a2" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP1046020348" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="margin-left:23.4pt; border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_flatness_3.gif" width="252px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs9" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_flatness_5.gif" width="241px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Flatness = 3</span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:center;" align="center"><span lang="EN-GB">Flatness = 5</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Minimum  triangles connected</b></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription"><span lang="EN-GB">Minimum number of neighbouring triangles selected. When you select by curvature, you get some groups of triangles selected forming isolated islands. With this minimum number of triangles, user can easily deselect these islands. Range of this parameter is from 0 to 10,000. Default values is Minimum 200 triangles connected.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a3" style="text-decoration:underline;">Example</a></span></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP222720847" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
<table class="TableGrid" style="margin-left:23.4pt; border-collapse:collapse; border-spacing:5px;" cellspacing="5">
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_triangles_1.gif" width="241px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs10" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../images/select_curvature_triangles_200.gif" width="243px" height="250px" border="0" class="img_whs11" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="middle" class="whs5">
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Minimum number of triangles connected = 1</span></p>
</td>
<td valign="top" class="whs6">
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">Minimum number of triangles connected = 200</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This selection tool is a mode, which means that it will stay on the left pane until you close it. During this time you can rotate, pan, and zoom the viewport in order to achieve better observation of the objects. Using spin buttons in the dialog you can adjust the parameters of the selection that you want to make. You can check at any time whether the selection satisfies you simply by pressing</span> <span class="Button">Select</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button. When you are ready, press</span> <span class="Button">Close</span> <span lang="EN-GB">button to exit</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Select By Curvature</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode. Note that</span> <span class="Command">Select By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">removes any previous mesh selections. Other data types remain unaffected.</span></p>
<p class="Use"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Use</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">that selection method to extract and process the features from an object. If you want to process flat areas, after</span> <span class="Command">Select By Curvature</span> <span lang="EN-GB">call</span> <span class="Command">Invert Selection</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command.</span></p>
